{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interfaceSelected_three_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interfaceSelected_three_ten","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L372-L385","doc":"**The pp bond `G³` is still selected among `m ≤ 10`**, and on the **wide** interval\n`1 < q ≤ 23/20`: only `G¹, G²` infeasible and `G³` feasible are needed, since every bond\nwith `m ≥ 3` costs at least six crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interface_frobeniusFeasible_iff_three_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interface_frobeniusFeasible_iff_three_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L352-L370","doc":"**Reading 3 on the `H₆` interface, `1 ≤ m ≤ 10`, `1 < q ≤ 10/9`: feasible iff `3 ∣ m`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interface_frobenius_table_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.interface_frobenius_table_ten","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L318-L350","doc":"**The `H₆` bond table for `m = 6..10`** on `1 < q ≤ 10/9`: `G⁶, G⁹` feasible,\n`G⁷, G⁸, G¹⁰` infeasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.frobeniusSelected_borromean_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.frobeniusSelected_borromean_ten","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L296-L310","doc":"**Reading 3 still selects `β_Bor` with candidates up to ten vertices**, for every\n`1 < q ≤ 23/20`: `k = 6, 9` are feasible but cost 12 and 18. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.vertexPow_frobeniusFeasible_iff_three_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.vertexPow_frobeniusFeasible_iff_three_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L277-L294","doc":"**Reading 3 on `H₃`, `1 ≤ k ≤ 10`: feasible iff `3 ∣ k`** — the survivors are the powers\nof the `q`-deformed 3-cycle `V³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.hoefsmit_vertexPow_frobenius_table_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.hoefsmit_vertexPow_frobenius_table_ten","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L256-L275","doc":"**The `H₃` table for `k = 6..10`**: `k = 6, 9` feasible, `k = 7, 8, 10` infeasible, for\nevery `1 < q ≤ 23/20` and every weight with `y_(2,1) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.hoefsmitVtx_traces_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.hoefsmitVtx_traces_ten","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L230-L254","doc":"The closed forms at the concrete Hoefsmit data, `k = 6..10`, `x = h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.h_sq_le_eighteenth_of_q_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.h_sq_le_eighteenth_of_q_le","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L211-L222","doc":"`1 ≤ q ≤ 10/9 ⇒ h² ≤ 1/18` (`h² ≤ 0.0446` there; the pin has `0.0437`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.h6_signs_six_to_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.h6_signs_six_to_ten","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L186-L209","doc":"The `(3,3)` condition `1 + 2χ_m`, `m = 6..10`, has signs `(+, −, −, +, −)` for every\n`0 < x ≤ 1/18`. (`1 + 2χ₈` changes sign near `x ≈ 0.0581`, so `1/12` is not enough.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.chi_signs_six_to_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.chi_signs_six_to_ten","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L162-L184","doc":"The signs `(+, −, −, +, −)` of `χ_6..χ_10` for every `0 < x ≤ 1/10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.pow_bounds_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.pow_bounds_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L131-L160","doc":"Power bounds used by the sign lemmas: `x^n ≤ x / c^(n-1)` for `0 < x ≤ 1/c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_ten","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L116-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_nine","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L108-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_eight","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L100-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_seven","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L92-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.trace_vtx_pow_six","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L85-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_ten","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L74-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_nine","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L69-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_eight","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L65-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_seven","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L61-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen.lin_six","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectionTen.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0}]}